WEBVTT

00:00:01.000 --> 00:00:05.500
The Netherlands is a northwestern European country famous for windmills, tulip fields, and canals.

00:00:06.000 --> 00:00:11.000
Over a quarter of Dutch land lies below sea level, protected by the historic Delta Works dikes.

00:00:11.500 --> 00:00:17.000
The Kinderdijk windmill network is a UNESCO heritage site built in the 1740s to drain water.

00:00:17.500 --> 00:00:23.000
Traditional attire features wooden Klompen clogs carved from sturdy willow and poplar timber.

00:00:23.500 --> 00:00:29.000
Famous culinary delicacies include Gouda wheels, Edam cheese, and sweet caramel Stroopwafels.

